            {
              "id": "59390091-9954-46d2-ad52-a29d0c78861d",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong><strong>The Interpersonal Neurobiology of Play : Brain-Building Interventions for Emotional Well-Being</strong></strong></em> was written by Joshua M. Epstein &amp; Robert Axtell originally published by The MIT Press, November 1994."
            },
            {
              "id": "f8b77dec-688c-487f-941f-9cc9809a2447",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "6bb6470f-7ef8-4f06-bbab-428d47324cf4",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>The mental health field has seen a significant shift in the past decade toward including a neuroscience perspective when designing clinical interventions. However, for many play therapists it has been challenging to apply this information in the context of play therapy. Here, Theresa Kestly teaches therapists how to understand the neurobiology of play experiences so the undeniable benefits of play therapy can be exploited to their fullest.<br></em>"
            },
            {
              "id": "a89d12a8-77a8-4c9a-bece-834602ab2b31",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
